{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/862844-how-iskar-became-an-unfettered-eshmaki-collector","id":862844,"title":"How Iskar became an Unfettered Eshmaki Collector","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-09T16:42:09-07:00","id":862844,"title":"How Iskar became an Unfettered Eshmaki Collector","content":"I have been storytelling a (mostly) solo chronicle revolving around a Mekhet vampire, Iris, and her strange incorporeal companion, Iskar. Me and my fiancee have played this chronicle for the last six years. When Beast came out, I realized something about Iskar and what he was. Short version follows...<br /> <br /> Iskar used to have a physical form, and used to put fear into the hearts of humans. He was known as the shadow being Izzakara (meaning &quot;saying&quot; in Sumerian), as his fear-mongering taught humans in Sumeria important lessons about life. He was also known as Anzu, the bird-like horror who drew the attention of a mighty champion, Ninurta. Ninurta, a hero of the humans, was upset that Anzu had stolen the Tablet of Destiny, and hunted down and killed the monster, as according to legend.<br /> <br /> Iskar did not die, however, as part of him survived, and he had now learned the lessons of the tablet. He continued his existence as an incorporeal being (but not quite a spirit), and spent a lot of time searching for the Dark Mother that spawned him, but also after treasures that he felt resonated with him. A collector, if you like. Some humans occasionally learned of him, and tried to capture him using the same Bane that Ninurta had used so long ago, but he always managed to get away.<br /> <br /> One day, he met a Mekhet vampire. They were distant kindred, and had the connection with the dark in common. Together, they had many adventures, searching for both treasures and information on the Dark Mother (or the Crone). He told Iris that the Mother was in a dream state, not quite awake in our world, but affecting it through nightmares.<br /> <br /> After a while, Iris also met another monster and a sister of Iskar. She was a being of the depths, and had a surreal, watery dominion, into which Iris could be invited, as long as there was enough water. That monster called herself Makara, and spoke with Iris of teaching humanity though fear, just as her brother Iskar had done before.<br /> <br /> Then I read Beast: the Primordial.<br /> <br /> So apparently Iskar and Makara are both Unfettered horrors of Eshmaki and Makara lineages. Who knew.<br /> <br /> What can I say. Great thinks mind alike.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5260-themangynimrod","name":"TheMangyNimrod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:19:04-07:00","id":862878,"title":"","content":"Don't the Unfettered Horrors have a simplistic mindset (i.e. Legend, Family and Hunger but no Life)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-09T17:55:22-07:00","id":862908,"title":"","content":"I should probably have mentioned that Iris is the player character and Iskar is an NPC <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> But yes, they are simplistic in terms of wants/needs in the same way a low rank spirit or ghost is. However, as Power increases (Intelligence is a Power trait), so might the methods change, and Iskar is very old and has a lot of Power. Iskar still hoards and searches for the Mother, but does so with more intricate plans. The tablet of destiny increased his cunning, as well. <br /> <br /> Furthermore, the point of my story was to mention the degree to which our creative processes converged, rather than focusing on &quot;hey, that's not exactly the same!&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5260,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5260-themangynimrod","user":"TheMangyNimrod","date":". 04-09-2016, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5260-themangynimrod","name":"TheMangyNimrod","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}